Acceleration [SimTalk] - Conveyor
Sets the Acceleration with which the Conveyor designated by <Path> increases its speed in m/s2.
Remarks
You can only set the Acceleration after you activate Acceleration/AccelerationEnabled.
Type
Attribute
Syntax
<Path>.Acceleration:acceleration
Watchable
The attribute is watchable.
Assignment Value
You can assign a value of data type acceleration.
Specify any real number greater than or equal to 0. The Conveyor accelerates until it has reached its final
Speed. It accelerates no matter if a MU is located on it or not until it reaches its final speed.
Note
In SimTalk 2.0 you can specify the acceleration units mps², cm², fps², and LU/s².
Type in the unit directly after the values, without a separating blank space, for example 10mps2 or
10.2mps2.
To create the ² symbol, activate the Num Lock key on the numeric keypad, hold down Alt and type in
0178 on the numeric keypad.
To create the ² symbol on the German keyboard layout, hold down Alt Gr and press the key with the
number 2. If your keyboard does not have the Alt Gr key, hold down Ctrl-right+Alt-right instead.
Example
MyConveyor.Acceleration := 3mps2
Acceleration [SimTalk] - Conveyor
Plant Simulation Help 11-2179
