Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

AutomaticStop [SimTalk] - Conveyor
Automatically stops the Conveyor designated by<Path>. This means that it sets the current speed to 0
when it does not transport a MU.
Remarks
Automatically stopping the Conveyor might, for example, be the case when it is empty or when it is
blocked when a part cannot leave it.
The Speed it set to 0 immediately without using the value for the Deceleration. Likewise, the Speed is set
to the Target Speed again immediately without using the value for the Acceleration.
If the speed of the Conveyor is 0, the Energy State changes to operational.
Type
Attribute
Syntax
<Path>.AutomaticStop:boolean
Assignment Value
You can assign a value of data type boolean.
Example
MyConveyor.AutomaticStop := true
See also
Automatic Stop [check box] - Conveyor
Operational [energy]
AutomaticStop [SimTalk] - Conveyor
Plant Simulation Help 11-2183
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

Backwards [SimTalk] - Conveyor
Sets if the Conveyor designated by <Path> and the MUs on it move in reverse (true) or forward (false).
Remarks
When moving in reverse the MUs enter the Conveyor at its exit and leave it at its entrance.
If you cleared Acceleration of the Conveyor, it reverses the direction in which it moves immediately
without decelerating and accelerating.
If you selected Acceleration, the Conveyor slows down until its speed is 0. Then it reverses the direction in
which it moves and accelerates until it reaches its final speed.
If you set a Target Distance for the Transporter, you cannot change the attribute Backwards.
Type
Attribute
Syntax
<Path>.Backwards:boolean
Assignment Value
You can assign a value of data type boolean.
Example
MyConveyor.Backwards := false
SimTalk
